# Tests for the bed centre singularity limits - the moves near the bed's
# rotation axis that are legal, and legal only slowly.  The moves that
# are refused outright are in polar_singularity_refuse.test, which needs
# a file of its own because SHOULD_FAIL applies to a whole test.
#
# Nothing here comes to rest on the axis.  A move that ends on it, or
# starts from it along a new ray, leaves the bed angle a free choice that
# nothing yet schedules - the C dead zone of kin_corertheta.c resolves
# such a sample from the direction of travel, which is right for the
# homing sweep it was written for and is a half turn commanded in one
# sample for anything else.  Scheduling that angle is the next stage of
# this work, and until it exists there is nothing here to assert.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG polar_singularity.cfg

# Home.  The R sweep runs along y == 0 at a fixed bed angle, so it is
# radial by construction and does not turn the bed at all - which is why
# it may start from a radius of zero.
G28 X
G28 B
G28 Z
G90

# Well clear of the centre: untouched at any feedrate the machine has
G1 X80 Y0 Z10 F6000
G1 X80 Y40 F6000
G1 X40 Y80 F6000
G1 X0 Y80 F6000

# Chords that pass near the centre.  Each is held to 5 * r_min mm/s
# whatever feedrate is asked for, so the F6000 below arrives as 200mm/s
# at a closest approach of 40mm, 25mm/s at 5mm and 5mm/s at 1mm.
G1 X40 Y-30 F6000
G1 X40 Y30 F6000

G1 X5 Y-20 F6000
G1 X5 Y20 F6000

G1 X1 Y-10 F6000
G1 X1 Y10 F6000

# The same on the other side of the axis, and at an angle to it
G1 X-1 Y10 F6000
G1 X-1 Y-10 F6000
G1 X-15 Y-15 F6000
G1 X-15 Y15 F6000
G1 X15 Y15 F6000

# Just inside the refusal threshold: a chord passing 0.15mm from the
# centre needs 0.75mm/s, which clears the 0.5mm/s floor
G1 X20 Y20 F3000
G1 X0.15 Y-10 F6000
G1 X0.15 Y10 F6000

# A quarter turn at a comfortable radius, then a half turn taken the
# long way round rather than across the middle
G1 X50 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y50 F3000
G1 X-50 Y0 F3000
G1 X0 Y-50 F3000
G1 X50 Y0 F3000

# Rotating the head near the centre does not turn the bed, so it is not
# limited by any of this
G1 X2 Y-8 F3000
G1 B20 F600
G1 B-20 F600
G1 B0 F600

# Printing near the centre still works, just slowly
G1 X20 Y0 Z0.3 F1500
G1 X2 Y-8 E1 F1500
G1 X2 Y8 E2 F1500
G1 X20 Y8 E3 F1500

GET_POSITION
M114
M84
